{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:43:17.931290Z","id":"1f1d83cfddbe3c98907366125e5d52e3977219be9dc8e4a5140d4306eade3a91","body":{"detail":"In the derive branch of `share_explicit`, `record_artifact` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:842-844) writes the cache record under `derived.provenance.id`, which the derivers normalise: Claude uses the session-chain head (crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:52-61, a successor-segment id maps to the head), Gemini uses `session_uuid` over the entry id (derive.rs:122-128), Codex resolves a partial UUID prefix to the rollout's full id (derive.rs:162-169, toolpath-codex `find_rollout_file` accepts a substring match at crates/toolpath-codex/src/paths.rs:118-130). `record_remotes` at cmd_share.rs:877-884 passes `session` instead, so `path share --session <successor|prefix|entry id>` leaves the cache record under one key and inserts a second known-but-uncached entry under the raw id via `record_remote`'s `or_insert_with` (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:110-125). Sync enumerates only the normalised id, so the stray entry is never materialised, and the chain-head entry that incremental append / `share --all` will consult carries no remote. The fast path (cmd_share.rs:784-789) is unaffected because `fresh_cache_id` only matches when `session` is already the manifest key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":873},"end":{"line":884},"content_hash":"5cda0306fb41a83e9e37d7c071cb05d728ac1a23de8819cd8f605e89aa58dabc"},"suggested_fix":"In the derive branch, record under `derived.provenance.as_ref().map(|p| (p.id.as_str(), p.path.as_deref()))`, falling back to `session`/`project` only when provenance is `None`; add a share test that passes a Claude successor-segment id (or a Codex prefix) and asserts the remote lands on the same entry as `cache_id`.","summary":"Derive-path share records the remote under the caller's `session` id, not the manifest id the cache record uses","tags":["review","review:pr-356-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:43:17.931385Z","id":"afcb76e8987fa3d8800c76ef780ea1e43ed552db89a78503307f89fa5987a827","body":{"detail":"`project_into_harness` collapses `ClaudeProjection::Written` and `ClaudeProjection::AlreadyLocal` into one `session_id` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs:677-683); `AlreadyLocal` means the local file was left untouched and 'may be newer than the shared document' (crates/path-cli/src/projection/claude.rs:10-13, 26-30). `record_pull` (cmd_resume.rs:223-285) then stats that untouched local file for `source_stamp` (lines 266-268) while `steps`/`last_step`/`head` come from the fetched path (line 269). The spec's stat gate skips a session whose stamp has not moved, so steps the local session already has beyond the fetched prefix would count as sent. `record_remote` replaces any earlier record at the URL (engine.rs:126), so a `--force` re-fetch of a session that was shared from this machine overwrites a correct share record with this one. Reproduce: `path share` a session, then `path resume --force <its url>` in the same project.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"341a7cb7862f3ff7023e9ea2fe4da0b07912c38d511c99544db4df827b4434da"},"suggested_fix":"Have `project_into_harness` return whether it wrote the session (or a `Projected { session_id, written: bool }`), and call `record_pull` only when `written` is true; alternatively skip the write when the session's manifest entry already has a record for that URL.","summary":"`record_pull` also runs when projection found an existing local session, pairing the fetched doc's `steps`/`head` with a possibly newer local stamp","tags":["review","review:pr-356-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:43:17.931488Z","id":"7340776360dd09e42bc06cb3f14514f74e02a586bd012fae0287fcf54559f2ae","body":{"detail":"`run_pathbase` reads the cache body at crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:872 and only after the upload returns calls `session_of_cache_id` (line 888), which takes `(rec.modified, rec.size)` from the manifest as it is then (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:483-494). A `p cache sync` (or a `path query` auto-sync) that re-derives the session between those two points rewrites the cache file and the record's stamp (`record_artifact`/`flush_writes`, engine.rs:252-269, 400-422) while the cache id stays the same (it is `make_id(type, path.id)`, derive.rs:84). The remote record then says the remote holds the derive at the new stamp although the old body was uploaded, and the spec's stat gate skips the session until the source moves again. The share paths avoid this by taking the stamp before the read (`fresh_cache_id` at cmd_share.rs:784; `claude_chain_stamp` before `read_conversation` at derive.rs:56-73).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":885},"end":{"line":892},"content_hash":"37405d03890c3001e59d6b5917d8eda946acc829c2d2ee492a1fa4506abbbc0f"},"suggested_fix":"Call `session_of_cache_id(&args.input)` before `std::fs::read_to_string(&file)` and carry the stamp through to `record_remotes`; or re-read it afterwards and skip the record when the two differ.","summary":"`p export pathbase <cache id>` reads the session's stamp after the upload, so a concurrent sync can stamp the record newer than the body that was sent","tags":["review","review:pr-356-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:43:17.931573Z","id":"2486d9fc48552c6fc5b0f95ffb6597973fa8fb4f4978218c4b8e199618ac6988","body":{"detail":"`remote_path_url` interpolates `base_url`, `owner`, `repo` and `graph_id` as given, trimming only a trailing slash. On push `base_url` is the stored credential URL or `resolve_url(--url)` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:951-963) and `graph_id` is `Uuid::to_string()` of the create response (cmd_pathbase.rs:588, lowercase hyphenated). On pull `base_url` is `format!(\"{scheme}{host}\")` from the URL exactly as the user typed it (crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:464) and `graph_id` is the raw `ref_.id` segment (cmd_resume.rs:261), which `extract_triple` accepts in any form `Uuid::parse_str` takes (derive.rs:488-491: uppercase, braces, no hyphens). Owner/repo from a URL are not percent-decoded before `encode_segment` re-encodes them (derive.rs:494-501 → cmd_pathbase.rs:84-86), so an already-encoded segment is double-encoded. Example: `path share` records `https://pathbase.dev/u/me/r/graphs/fe94b6f9-.../paths/...`; `path resume https://PATHBASE.DEV/u/me/r/graphs/FE94B6F9-.../` records a second key for the same path. The client base also differs from the server's `public_url` whenever the client reaches the server through another host (the server's own URL for the graph is `created.url`, pathbase `crates/pathbase-api/src/responses.rs:109-112`).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":88},"content_hash":"a6caa163c5805bc004c314d4b0fe25641f3439e9d58a3954af30c52f8786bfda"},"suggested_fix":"Canonicalise inside `remote_path_url`: lowercase scheme and host, take the graph id as a `uuid::Uuid` (both call sites already have one) and render it with `to_string()`, and percent-decode URL segments in `extract_triple` before they are re-encoded. Add a test that the key from a typed-URL pull equals the key from a credential-URL push for the same graph.","summary":"Push and pull build the record key from differently-normalised inputs, so one path can get two keys","tags":["review","review:pr-356-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:43:17.931631Z","id":"c1304b44445471c14d4a19295c87809a9b1446e016409bd637962e2a029261e9","body":{"detail":"`resolve_input` sets `fetched` only in the network branch (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs:453); the cache-hit branch (lines 431-440) leaves it `None`, and `run_with_strategy` records nothing (lines 210-212). The projected Claude session id is derived from the path, not minted per run (crates/path-cli/src/projection/claude.rs:25-35), so a second `path resume <url>` in the same project resolves to `AlreadyLocal` and keeps the first run's record; but the same URL resumed in a different project directory, or any harness whose projection mints a fresh id, produces a new session with no `remotes` entry. The spec (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-07-path-parent-and-delegation-design.md § Remote records, pathbase repo) says a pull creates the record so that 'work done in the resumed session then appends to that path instead of creating a new graph'; for every resume after the first that outcome does not hold. Only the server id lookup needs the network, and `graph_paths_list` is already a separate call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":431},"end":{"line":440},"content_hash":"d6d66a3575f7e8d794be1d06381503914a7dba4bab5ab8a8700b9221e3f11a1a"},"suggested_fix":"Record on cache hits too: set `fetched` in both branches (the cached document still came from `base_url`/`ref_`), and let `record_pull` make its one `GET …/graphs/{id}/paths` request, warning and continuing offline as it already does on error. Add a test for the cached-resume case.","summary":"A resume served from the cache writes no remote record, so a second resume of the same URL into another project cannot append to the path","tags":["review","review:pr-356-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:43:17.931710Z","id":"1476309721fcd6900c43c2d9c968a7ad8546ba46b184b3046871dff6aaadd8f5","body":{"detail":"`relax_for_older_servers` (crates/pathbase-client/build.rs:85-105) makes `GraphCreatedResponse.paths` optional so an older server's response decodes with `paths: []`. `uploaded_paths` then yields an empty list (cmd_export.rs:979-988), and `record_remotes` finds no URL for any path and `continue`s (lines 927-935) without a message. The CHANGELOG entry for 0.30.0 tells users every successful `path share`/`p export pathbase` writes a record; against such a server none is written and nothing says so, and once incremental append reads these records every share against that server will open a new graph. The pull side already warns in the analogous case (`graph_paths_list` returns no match, cmd_resume.rs:253-259).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":910},"end":{"line":942},"content_hash":"61c87f8de46b135d7b6af47ea992010512db50f205955a6cc1103429b9b4e009"},"suggested_fix":"In `record_remotes`, when `doc` has at least one inline path with steps but `uploaded` is empty, `eprintln!` one warning naming the server as not reporting stored paths; the test `share_from_the_cache_records_the_upload` (cmd_share.rs) can assert it.","summary":"An upload whose create response lists no paths records nothing silently; warn when the document had inline paths","tags":["review","review:pr-356-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:51:41.195633Z","id":"25f3a36bb1f187aa8b82bbd9e79d9d38a518534d6cb610ac8146e8026c67dc14","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:871-873 reads the cache body; :885 runs the upload; only then does :888 call `crate::sync::session_of_cache_id(&args.input)`, which returns `(rec.modified, rec.size)` from the manifest as it is at that moment (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:483-494). A concurrent `p cache sync` overwrites the same cache file (`write_cached(&derived.cache_id, ..., true)`, engine.rs:363) and the record's `modified`/`size` (engine.rs:364-377 staged, :253-269 flushed via `put_record` :244-249, which keeps `remotes`), and the cache id is unchanged because it is `make_id(ArtifactType::Claude.name(), &path.path.id)` (crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:84). The record written at :891 then carries the newer stamp with the older body's `steps`/`last_step`, and the stat gate (spec: source_stamp skips a session whose stamp has not moved) skips it. `share_explicit` takes the stamp before the read (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:784 `fresh_cache_id`, :871-876 provenance stamp), so the two paths are inconsistent. A timing-dependent race with no deterministic repro: `concern` is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"7340776360dd09e42bc06cb3f14514f74e02a586bd012fae0287fcf54559f2ae","summary":"confirmed: the stamp is read from the manifest after the upload, so a sync between the body read and that lookup stamps the record newer than the uploaded body","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:51:41.195710Z","id":"6f2b7df9c776921f0f9c2be576a8f71dd7a356b6f662b27def389fe8ec53a841","body":{"detail":"crates/pathbase-client/build.rs:91-104 drops `paths` from `GraphCreatedResponse`'s required list, so an older server's response decodes with an empty vector (test `graphs_post_accepts_a_response_without_paths`, crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs:1516-1532 asserts `created.paths.is_empty()`). `run_pathbase_inner` returns `uploaded_paths(.., &created.paths)` / `&resp.paths` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:1015, :1086), and `record_remotes` :929-935 `continue`s per path with no output when no URL matches. No warning exists between :910-945, nor in `run_pathbase_inner` :966-1087. The streamed route is unaffected (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs:852-857 fills `created.paths` from the per-path open responses), so this is only the `body.len() <= BATCH_BUDGET || !streamable` branch (:1037-1046) and the anon route (:997-1015). CHANGELOG.md:12-14 promises a record after every successful `path share`/`p export pathbase`. `cmd_resume.rs:254-260` does warn in the analogous pull case. Kind `suggestion` fits: nothing breaks today since nothing reads the records yet (engine.rs:60-61).","kind":"comment","references":"1476309721fcd6900c43c2d9c968a7ad8546ba46b184b3046871dff6aaadd8f5","summary":"confirmed: a create response with no `paths` records nothing and prints nothing on the single-request and anonymous routes","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:51:41.195733Z","id":"931a657b1c34e064b49d32f3cea8c4f5dc0b2ba41bd11f5f189c6492b133488b","body":{"detail":"`remote_path_url` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_pathbase.rs:73-87) only trims a trailing slash from `base_url` and interpolates `graph_id` as given. Push: `graph_id` is `inner.id.to_string()` of a `format: uuid` field (cmd_pathbase.rs:516, :588; openapi.json `Graph.properties.id` is `{type: string, format: uuid}`), i.e. lowercase hyphenated, and `base_url` is the stored credential URL (cmd_export.rs:957-961). Pull: `parse_pathbase_ref` returns `format!(\"{scheme}{host}\")` with the host exactly as typed (crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:450-464, no lowercasing), and `extract_triple` keeps the id segment as a string after only checking `Uuid::parse_str(id).is_err()` (derive.rs:488-491, :509); `Uuid::parse_str` accepts simple, hyphenated, braced and `urn:uuid:` forms (https://docs.rs/uuid/latest/uuid/struct.Uuid.html#method.parse_str). `record_pull` passes that raw `&ref_.id` to `remote_path_url` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs:261) even though `graph_paths_list` parses it to a `Uuid` for the request one line earlier (cmd_pathbase.rs:1122-1126). Owner/repo segments are never percent-decoded (derive.rs:494-510) before `encode_segment` re-encodes them (cmd_pathbase.rs:84-85). So `path resume https://PATHBASE.DEV/u/me/r/graphs/FE94B6F9-.../` yields a different key than the push for the same path. Nothing reads the keys yet, so no user-visible failure before merge: `concern` is right.","kind":"comment","references":"2486d9fc48552c6fc5b0f95ffb6597973fa8fb4f4978218c4b8e199618ac6988","summary":"confirmed: pull keys use the typed URL's host and raw graph-id segment while push keys use the credential URL and `Uuid::to_string()`, so the same path can get two keys","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:51:41.195747Z","id":"b8ef116eec3022bd181ed2ff5ca6a9771b9b56500d369d2516a1a7f6697d94ad","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs:209-212 calls `record_pull` whenever `fetched` is set, regardless of how `project_into_harness` resolved; :676-683 collapse `Written` and `AlreadyLocal` into one `session_id`. `AlreadyLocal` means nothing was written and the local copy 'may be newer than the shared document' (crates/path-cli/src/projection/claude.rs:7-14, :26-30). `record_pull` then stats the local session (cmd_resume.rs:266-268) and takes `steps`/`last_step`/`head` from the fetched `path` (:269, `RemoteRecord::of`), and `record_remote` does `remotes.insert(url, record)`, replacing any earlier record under that URL (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:109-131). The projected session id is the original session id carried in the artifact key (`claude-code://<session>`, crates/toolpath-convo/src/extract.rs:139-146 sets `view.id`), so `path share` of session X followed by `path resume --force <its url>` in the same project resolves to `AlreadyLocal { X }` and overwrites X's share record with one whose `steps` is the fetched prefix but whose stamp is the current local file's. Only matters once incremental append reads the records (engine.rs:60-61), so `concern` is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"afcb76e8987fa3d8800c76ef780ea1e43ed552db89a78503307f89fa5987a827","summary":"confirmed: `record_pull` runs for `AlreadyLocal` too, pairing the fetched path's steps with the untouched local file's stamp and replacing any share record at that URL","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:51:41.195759Z","id":"7c55e64db6d5f732a1f0b69a46f404e4467cacd41813762ec9c8c3beb55205e4","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_resume.rs:421 initialises `fetched = None`; the cache-hit branch :431-440 returns the cached JSON without touching it; only the network branch sets it (:453). `run_with_strategy` records only `if let Some(fetched) = &fetched` (:210-212). The projected Claude session id is a function of the path (crates/toolpath-convo/src/extract.rs:139-146; crates/path-cli/src/projection/claude.rs:25-35), so resuming the same URL in a different project directory takes the `Written` branch (claude.rs:26-35, the session file does not exist under that project dir) and the new session has no `remotes` entry. The spec requires a pull to create the record so that work in the resumed session 'appends to that path instead of creating a new graph' (/Users/ben/empathic/oss/pathbase/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-07-path-parent-and-delegation-design.md:246-250). `record_pull` only needs `base_url`/`ref_`, both available in the cache-hit branch (:429), and its one request is `graph_paths_list` (:237-243) with an offline warning path (:249-252). Nothing consumes the records yet, so `concern` is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"c1304b44445471c14d4a19295c87809a9b1446e016409bd637962e2a029261e9","summary":"confirmed: the cache-hit branch leaves `fetched` as `None`, so a resume served from the cache writes no remote record","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T19:51:41.195774Z","id":"ef7afc3bcabc31c32c033ee977893336d1cfdbae9d5cc61e49969261a6e436d4","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:842-844 calls `record_artifact(&config, stub, &derived.cache_id)` with `stub = derived.provenance`, whose `id` the derivers normalise: Claude to the chain head (`session_chain(..).into_iter().next()`, crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:56-61, :90), Gemini to `session_uuid` over the entry id (derive.rs:120-128), Codex to the full id of the matched rollout file (derive.rs:162-169). `record_remotes` at cmd_share.rs:877-884 passes `session` instead. `record_remote` keys the manifest by that `id` and `or_insert_with` creates a known-but-uncached `SyncRecord` when it is absent (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:117-131), so a share by a non-canonical id yields two entries: the canonical one with `cache_id` and no remotes, and a stray one with the remote and `cache_id: None`. The fast path is unaffected since `fresh_cache_id` looks up `manifest.get(type)?.get(id)?` by the caller's id and needs `cache_id` (engine.rs:468-469). Kind `concern` fits: the upload succeeds and nothing reads the records yet.","kind":"comment","references":"1f1d83cfddbe3c98907366125e5d52e3977219be9dc8e4a5140d4306eade3a91","summary":"confirmed: the derive branch records the cache under `derived.provenance.id` but the remote under the caller's raw `session`, which differ for successor-segment, entry and prefix ids","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
